            {
              "name": "JavaScriptCore and WebKit, in Bun's fork",
              "version": "commit 2e2aa2290fac856d6f451ceacb58f7f5b44dd057",
              "license": "LGPL-2.0-or-later and LGPL-2.1-or-later (per file), and BSD-style licences",
              "source": "https://github.com/oven-sh/WebKit/tree/2e2aa2290fac856d6f451ceacb58f7f5b44dd057",
              "notes": [
                "Bun links JavaScriptCore statically, so the gbrain binary contains it. To use a modified JavaScriptCore: build Bun 1.4.2 from its source with your WebKit (Bun's licence file above gives the steps), build GBrain from its source at the commit above with that Bun (bun build --compile), sign the result ad hoc (codesign --force --sign - <file>) and put it at local-brain/bin/gbrain. Atum runs that binary only if its size and SHA-256 match the \"signed\" entry of local-brain/SIGNED-BINARY.json, so record the new size and SHA-256 there, then re-sign Atum ad hoc (codesign --force --deep --sign - <path of the Atum app>)."
              ],
              "licenseFiles": [
                "texts/LGPL-2.0.txt",
                "texts/LGPL-2.1.txt"
              ]
